.\" Manpage for quanuxctl probe
.\" Contact quanux@foundation.local
.TH QUANUXCTL-PROBE 8 "February 2026" "QuanuX v0.1.0" "QuanuX Command Manual"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-probe \- Neural Tap diagnostic stethoscope and surgical kit for QuanuX nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl probe
[\fB\-\-fix\fR] [\fB\-\-watchdog\fR | \fB\-w\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBquanuxctl probe\fR command embodies Operation "Neural Tap". It serves as the primary diagnostic tool for a QuanuX Execution Node, evaluating the three physical layers of Node Sovereignty.
.PP
Furthermore, the \fBFast-Nerve\fR Watchdog Receptor runs persistently as a systemd service (\fBquanux-nerve.service\fR), exposing a FastAPI REST interface on port \fB8080\fR to assess and trigger these diagnostics remotely.
.B The Bone (OS/Environment)
Audits the `conda` environment (quanux-node) and ensures the `set-quanux-node` binary is present in the active PATH.
.TP
.B The Nerve (NATS Connectivity)
Validates local memory-mapped communication (NATS Port 4222) and cluster handshaking routes (Port 6222). Confirms at least one active peer route.
.TP
.B The Soul (Security/Identity)
Verifies the existence of 4096-bit RSA identity keys and Ed25519 NKeys. Strictly enforces 600 permissions to prevent rejection by the NATS server.
.SH OPTIONS (CLI)
.TP
.BR \-\-fix
Executes the "Auto-Suture" Protocol locally. Attempts to repair any failing layer autonomously.
.SH FAST-NERVE REST API
The \fBquanux-nerve.service\fR runs a persistent ASGI gateway on port \fB8080\fR. 
.TP
.B GET /probe
Executes a passive Neural Tap and returns a JSON payload detailing the Sovereignty Status.
.TP
.B POST /nudge
Forces an asynchronous Auto-Suture cycle. Alternatively triggered via NATS subject \fBQUANUX.NODE.PROBE.<HOSTNAME>\fR.
.TP
.B GET /logs
Streams the tail of the Black Box fix log (\fI/var/log/quanux/fix.log\fR).
.TP
.B PUT /config/logging
Restricts the historian's persistence on the fly (e.g., {"max_bytes": 10485760, "backup_count": 5}). Writes to \fI/etc/quanux/logging.conf\fR.
.SH EXIT CODES (CLI)
The Apoptoic Avoidance protocol expects one of the following terminal exit states:
.TP
\fB0\fR
\fBSovereign (Nominal)\fR \- All layers operational.
.TP
\fB1\fR
\fBIsolated\fR \- Nerve failure. NATS cluster routes are unresponsive or isolated from peers.
.TP
\fB2\fR
\fBNutrient Deficiency\fR \- Bone failure. The conda environment is corrupt or strictly required binaries are absent.
.TP
\fB3\fR
\fBIdentity Crisis\fR \- Soul failure. Invalid or exposed RSA/NKey files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a standard diagnostic tap:
.RS 4
$ quanuxctl probe
.RE
.PP
Attempt a system-wide diagnosis and Auto-Suture repair:
.RS 4
$ quanuxctl probe --fix
.RE
.PP
Engage the persistent Watchdog Receptor:
.RS 4
$ quanuxctl probe --watchdog
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quanuxctl (1),
